{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subgraph of a graph, as a lazy view: some of its vertices and some of its edges, renumbered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"densely. Made by "},{"code":"inducedSubgraph(on:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"spanningSubgraph(edges:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"subgraph(vertices:edges:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (NetworkX’s "},{"code":"subgraph_view","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT’s "},{"code":"AsSubgraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"SubDigraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", Boost’s "},{"code":"filtered_graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeIndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/UndirectedEdges"],"generated":true,"title":"Structures"},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/base"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties"},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations"],"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations"}],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","title":"SubgraphView","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}],"modules":[{"name":"GraphOperations"}],"externalID":"s:15GraphOperations12SubgraphViewV","remoteSource":{"fileName":"SubgraphView.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView.swift#L29"},"role":"symbol"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Base"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertices"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" are the kept vertices in the base’s order, at view indices ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"view keeps two arrays, base index to view index and back, so a row is the base’s row filtered","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and renumbered with one array load per entry and no hashing. A spanning subgraph keeps every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex at its base index.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edges"}]},{"type":"text","text":" keep the base’s positions, so a weight closure keyed by the base’s positions works"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on the view. An edge is in the view when both its ends are, and, if an edge set was given,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when it is in the set. With an edge set the view has dense edge indices: an edge’s index is its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rank among the kept edges in base order. Over a base with edge indices the set is a bit mask"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a count per 64-bit word, so the rank costs one popcount. Over a base without them (an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", a complement, an induced subgraph) the set is the sorted kept positions, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a row entry or a rank costs a binary search. An induced subgraph has no edge indices: building"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its edge mask would cost O(m). One on every vertex keeps the base’s rows, edge indices and flat"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rows."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The view holds a copy of the base (value semantics), so mutating the original never shows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through. Phase 1 needs a base with vertex indices; a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" with vertex holes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"traps at construction."}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://GraphOperations/s8CopyableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8CopyableP","title":"Swift.Copyable","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations":{"abstract":[],"role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph Implementations","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph-implementations","type":"topic"},"doc://GraphOperations/s9EscapableP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Escapable","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of directed edges between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"DirectedGraph","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"},"doc://GraphProtocol